posts.body:
Answering this here~
Psychoholic42 said:
I'm using a plugin that has a problem. The plugin skips the party command. The problem is, it takes away the escape option. I'm trying to make a skill that lets players escape, but can't get it to work. The best I can get is where the battle music continues after I escape.
Here is the plugin I'm using.
/*:
* @target MZ
* @plugindesc No party command (Fight, Escape) for TPB system.
*
@Author
Caethyril
* @url
https://forums.rpgmakerweb.com/threads/176490/
*
@Help
Free to use and/or modify for any project, no credit required.
*/
// Patch - cycle actors, skipping party command.
void (alias => {
BattleManager.selectPreviousCommand = function() {
alias.apply(this, arguments);
if (this._inputting && !this.actor())
this.changeCurrentActor(true);
};
})(BattleManager.selectPreviousCommand);
// Patch - reset flag to false to block turn-0 party command.
void (alias => {
BattleManager.initMembers = function() {
alias.apply(this, arguments);
this._tpbNeedsPartyCommand = false;
};
})(BattleManager.initMembers);
// Override - in TPB-Wait mode, allow multiple actors to be charged at once.
Game_Actor.prototype.shouldDelayTpbCharge = function() { return false; };
As for other plugins that might conflict with the plugin, I have a good number of them that I'm using. I did try to run your plugin alone to see if I had the same problem, and a different problem came up. After the last party member left, it froze and only showed the character's face at the bottom.
