Here's a link to the post where I shared this code:
Skip Party Command
I'm looking for a way to disable the party command in the battles. I'm using a plugin by Zevia called  SkipPartyMenu. The problem is that when the party command would normally come the game crashes with this error.
forums.rpgmakerweb.com
Maybe I'm missing something, but I just tested again and it seems to work OK for me. I tried playing a BGM on the map, entering battle via Battle Processing, then making everyone run away using a skill with an Escape effect on it. The battle ended as expected and the map BGM was reinstated. This test was successful with core script versions 1.9.0 and 1.10.0.
This makes sense to me, because by default my code only impacts things affecting player input. So I suspect it's conflicting with either another plugin or a core script edit, or there's something else you're doing (e.g. an unusual script call, a Parallel event that plays BGM, etc) that you haven't mentioned. Ideas:
With all plugins turned off in the Plugin Manager,
save your project
to apply Plugin Manager changes before testing. Otherwise the changes will not be respected, because the editor does not maintain a temporary "test" version of
plugins.js
.
From the editor's menu bar, choose
Game -> Update Corescript
. Pick a version and click OK. This should ensure your project is running on a clean (i.e. no edits) version of the core scripts.
As can be seen in the linked thread, this plugin of mine was specifically written for MZ's TPB system. If you've changed which battle system you're using, via the editor and/or plugins, you may well need a different plugin.
Otherwise, consider providing precise instructions on how to reproduce the problem, starting with "create a new project".
